# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Limpios Cleaning — environment variables
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. NEVER commit real keys (.env* is gitignored).
# In dev with no RESEND_API_KEY, lead submissions are logged to the server
# console and the UI still shows success — nothing breaks without these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Resend API key for sending lead-notification emails.
# Get one at https://resend.com. Leave blank for local dev (console logging).
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Inbox that receives new quote requests (defaults to info@limpioscleaning.com).
LEAD_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=info@limpioscleaning.com

# "From" sender for lead emails. Must be a verified domain sender in production.
# TODO: replace with e.g. "Limpios Cleaning <quotes@limpioscleaning.com>".
LEAD_FROM_EMAIL="Limpios Cleaning <onboarding@resend.dev>"

# Optional Google Analytics 4 measurement ID (e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX).
# Leave blank to disable GA. Vercel Analytics works without any key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# Optional Microsoft Clarity project ID (free heatmaps + session recordings).
# Get one at https://clarity.microsoft.com. Leave blank to disable Clarity.
# Privacy: Clarity records masked session replays; the footer carries the
# analytics disclosure. A consent banner isn't legally required for a small FL
# service business — gate the script behind consent if that ever changes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Durable lead store + rate limiting (Upstash Redis / Vercel KV).
# STRONGLY RECOMMENDED in production: with these set, every lead is persisted
# before the email send, so a Resend outage never drops a lead, and rate
# limiting becomes global (per-IP sliding window). Without them, leads are only
# console-logged and rate limiting is best-effort in-memory (per instance).
# Provision via Vercel Marketplace (Upstash) or upstash.com. Either naming works:
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# (Vercel KV integration also sets KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN, which
#  this app reads as a fallback — no extra config needed.)
